# nvim on a C file: the workloads of the JIM review (2026-10-09)
mark open
wait 2500
mark ctrl-d
repeat 8 300 \x04
mark ctrl-u
repeat 8 300 \x15
mark j-held
repeat 120 33 j
wait 500
mark insert
keys 300 o
keys 110 if (x == 42) { printf("the quick brown fox\n"); }
keys 300 \x1b
wait 300
mark split
keys 120 :split\r
wait 600
keys 120 :vsplit\r
wait 600
repeat 30 33 j
keys 200 \x17w
repeat 30 33 k
wait 300
mark quit
keys 120 :qa!\r
wait 800
